  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ footer cta */

  /* isolation gives the section its own stacking context, so the glow layer
     below can sit at -1: above the page ground, behind every word. */
  .section--cta {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
  }

  /* The footer glow moves onto its own layer so it can swell on approach
     instead of sitting at full strength from the section's first pixel. With
     no script it renders exactly as it did before: fully lit. */
  .cta-glow {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    background: var(--footer-glow);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .section--cta .inner {
    padding-top: 72px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }

  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-18);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta h2 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure-footer);
    font-size: clamp(26px, 5.5vw, var(--fs-h2));
    font-weight: var(--fw-black);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-h2-footer);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .cta-caption {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------- motion */

  /*
    The page's motion language is light, not movement: things glow on rather
    than slide around.

    Every resting state below is gated on html[data-motion], which the inline
    script at the top of the page sets during parse, and only when scripting is
    on and no reduced-motion request is in force. With the attribute absent
    this whole block does nothing and the page is the static page: nothing
    hidden, nothing animated, no stem. That is the reduced-motion contract, and
    it is one condition rather than a second copy of the stylesheet.

    Only transform, opacity and filter animate. Nothing runs longer than 300ms
    except the four ambient or scroll-linked beats, which are not states
    anything waits on: the stem, the light travelling the demo frame, the light
    arriving behind a section, and the drifting spores.

    Three of those glow. None of them rests lit for its own sake. The frame's
    highlight only exists while the panel is on screen and its position is
    scroll progress through that section, so it is a moving light and never a
    halo. A section's ambient light is a translucent wash that grows once as the
    section arrives and then holds as ground, at the same alpha the token sheet
    already uses for the footer. The spores are always moving and always under
    the content. Nothing here paints a coloured shadow at rest.

    The easing is written out rather than tokenised because the token sheet
    deliberately holds no motion values, and the rest of this file already
    spells the same curve out at every use.
